description:
import/rnews.rs:106–111: the cunbatch arm calls decompress_cunbatch() purely to produce its Err, then immediately has unreachable!(). This is harder to read than a direct return.

    } else if input.starts_with(CUNBATCH_MARKER) {
        decompress_cunbatch(&input[CUNBATCH_MARKER.len()..])?;
        unreachable!()
    }

Because decompress_cunbatch always returns Err, the ? propagates and the unreachable! is dead. But a reader has to understand all of that to follow the control flow.

Suggested approach: return the error directly without the indirection:

    } else if input.starts_with(CUNBATCH_MARKER) {
        return Err(RnewsError::UnsupportedCompression(
            "cunbatch (Unix compress .Z) is not supported; use gunbatch (gzip) instead".to_string(),
        ));
    }

decompress_cunbatch can remain as its own public entry point for callers who have a bare cunbatch payload. parse_rnews_batch need not route through it.
